course: dictionary
lesson: 16190
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Zulu is one word that can name people, a language, a letter, and a time. To know which meaning is right, read the clues around it: the words and sentences near it are its context.
explain: «Thandi speaks Zulu with her family at home.» Speaking is something you do with a language, so here Zulu means a language. «The pilot spelled the letter out: "Z for Zulu."» Spelling a letter is the clue, so here Zulu means the letter Z.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. Capital letters can help too: Zulu with a capital Z is the name of a people, a language, or a spelling word.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word. Context clues tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: «Zulu» can name a people, their language, a letter in the spelling alphabet, or a time.
fact: The Zulu are a large people of southern Africa, living mostly in South Africa, especially KwaZulu-Natal.
fact: isiZulu, also called Zulu, is the most widely spoken home language in South Africa.
fact: In the spelling alphabet, Zulu stands for the letter Z: «Alpha, Bravo ... Yankee, Zulu.» Zulu time means world standard time, also called UTC.
exercise: «The Zulu people have a long history in southern Africa.» What is Zulu in this sentence? | A letter of the alphabet | A type of bird | *A people | A kind of train
exercise: «The pilot spelled the letter out: "Z for Zulu."» What does Zulu stand for here? | The name of a river | A town in Africa | A large car | *The letter Z in the spelling alphabet
exercise: Maya says Zulu must be a food because it starts with a capital letter. What is the best answer? | Zulu is the name of a food, so Maya is right | Zulu only means a letter, so capitals are never used | Zulu is always a city in South Africa | *Capital letters do not mean food, but Zulu can name a people, a language, a letter, or a time
test: «Thandi speaks Zulu with her family at home.» What is Zulu in this sentence? | A city | A time | *A language | A letter
test: «The plane landed at ten o'clock Zulu time.» What does Zulu time mean? | The Zulu king | A kind of plane | *World standard time, also called UTC | A dance from South Africa
exam: «In history we learned about King Shaka and the Zulu kingdom.» Which meaning of Zulu fits here? | A letter of the alphabet | *A people | A language spoken by the pilot | A time on the clock
